---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How to Use the Free Exam Timer — Setup Guide for Teachers & Invigilators | FreeExamTimer"
  description="Step-by-step guide to setting up FreeExamTimer: writing time presets, reading time countdown, +25% extra time, full-screen hall display, chimes, and keyboard shortcuts."
  canonicalUrl="https://freeexamtimer.com/how-to/"
>
  <Nav active="how-to" />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-5 pt-24 pb-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-[40px] leading-[44px] font-semibold tracking-[-2px]">How to run an exam on this timer</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-6 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
      This site is only an exam clock. There is no stopwatch or alarm — just the controls an invigilator needs in a hall.
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8">
      <li>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium">1. Set writing time and use presets</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-5 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Enter hours, minutes, and seconds, or tap one-touch presets from 15 min through 3 hours. This is the official writing time, exclusive of reading time.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium">2. Reading time countdown</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-5 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Quickly select 5, 10, or 15 minutes of reading time. The timer clearly labels the reading phase and warns candidates not to write, before automatically transitioning into writing time with an audible chime.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium">3. Dual Finish Clocks & 25% Extra Time</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-5 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Tap "+25% Calc" to automatically calculate standard access arrangement extra time. The clock display presents both standard finish time and +25% extra finish time simultaneously, eliminating mental math in the exam hall. You can also add +5 or +15 minutes on the fly.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium">4. Candidate instructions & rules</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-5 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Add paper details and click quick rule chips (Silence at all times, No mobile phones, Black pen only) to project clean instructions throughout the examination.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium">5. Projector Hall Mode (F key)</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-5 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Press F or the full-screen icon to project a giant high-contrast clock readable from 30+ meters away. Controls auto-dim to minimize candidate distraction.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium">6. Chimes, warnings, and anxiety reduction</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-5 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Configure warnings (30m, 15m, 10m, 5m, 1m) with authentic Web Audio bells, gongs, or chimes. Enable "Hide seconds until final 5m" in Settings to keep anxious candidates calm during long papers.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="card mt-12 p-6">
      <p class="font-medium">Backup clock</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-5 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
        Do not rely on a single device. Keep a wall clock or second timer as backup. This page continues the exam if you refresh, but it cannot run if the computer sleeps without wake lock, or if the tab is discarded.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/" class="btn-pill mt-10 inline-flex">Open exam timer</a>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
